# ============================================================================
# LINE ENDINGS
#
# Every line in a text file ends with an invisible marker. Windows tools write
# two characters (CR+LF), everything else writes one (LF). Both work fine — the
# game does not care, node does not care, python does not care. Git cares,
# because a tool that rewrites the markers rewrites EVERY line, so a one-line
# edit shows up as a whole-file change and buries the real edit.
#
# With no rule here, whichever tool touched a file last decided its endings, and
# this repo drifted: 25 files CRLF, 13 LF, and 3 mixed inside themselves. The
# line below settles it — text files are stored in the repo as LF no matter what
# your editor writes locally, which is the convention GitHub and every web
# toolchain expects.
# ============================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one real exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse them with LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# ============================================================================
# BINARY — never rewrite these bytes, and never try to diff them as text.
# Models and textures would be CORRUPTED by line-ending translation, so they are
# named explicitly rather than left to git's content guess.
# ============================================================================
*.glb     binary
*.glb.bak binary
*.ktx2    binary
*.basis   binary

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary

*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.eot     binary

*.mp3     binary
*.ogg     binary
*.wav     binary
*.m4a     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.webm    binary

*.zip     binary
*.pdf     binary
